-- ind-a-tests-ambiguous.l4: assertions of ind-a that FAIL against the encoding where the SOURCE admits both answers.
-- Each assertion states MY expected answer (WORK/ind-a/expectations.md); its failure is the finding. None has been edited to match the code.
-- The count is kept in the header and in the final report. EXPECTED FAILING OR REFUSING ASSERTIONS IN THIS FILE: 9 (4 fail: AMB-5 to AMB-8; 5 refuse: AMB-1 to AMB-4 and AMB-9).

§ `ind-a: assertions that disagree with the encoding where the source is ambiguous`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Vintage of the text`
`ind-a amb vintage on` d MEANS `Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` d `the favoured interpretation`

-- AMB-1 (S1-16, C3, AMBIG-SRC). Expected: on 2014-11-21 "Minister" means the Chief Minister, because R&O.40/2019 Sch 2 para 1(e) substitutes FOR the words "Chief Minister"
-- and the Table of Legislation History lists no earlier amendment. The encoding REFUSES (no consolidated text before 1 January 2019 is among the sources).
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`ind-a amb vintage on` (YMD 2014 11 21)) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`

-- AMB-2 (S1-17). Expected: on 2018-05-01 the Chief Minister. The encoding REFUSES, as above.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`ind-a amb vintage on` (YMD 2018 5 1)) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`

-- AMB-3 (S1-34). Expected: on 2014-11-21 "Comptroller" has the meaning given by the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961 (L.13/2019 Sch 3 para 1 substitutes for those words). The encoding REFUSES.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` (`ind-a amb vintage on` (YMD 2014 11 21)) EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`

-- AMB-4 (SC-01 with S2.1-11). Expected: Articles 1 to 7 are in force from 21 November 2014, so on 2018-05-01 a Jersey company is an entity within 2(1)(f). The encoding REFUSES for every day before 1 January 2019.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`ind-a amb vintage on` (YMD 2018 5 1)) `ind-a Jersey company body` EQUALS LIST `a company`

-- AMB-5 (S2.1-09). Expected: a foundation is within (d) only. The encoding (F1.8 reading "as written", taken) also puts it in (g), "a body incorporated under, but not by, any enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991".
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `ind-a Jersey foundation body` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`

-- AMB-6 (S2.1-08). Expected: an incorporated 1862 association is within (c) only. The encoding also puts it in (g), as AMB-5.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `ind-a 1862 association` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`

-- AMB-7 (S8.3a-03 composed with S2.1-09). Expected: the note of status of a registered foundation needs no Article 8(3)(a)(ii) details (it is not within (e), (g), (h) or (j)).
-- Composed with G1's favoured reading the foundation is also (g), and G3 then requires (g) details for it.
#ASSERT null ((`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` `ind-a amb R` (`Art 2 the body as an entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` "Hope Foundation" `entered in the general section` EMPTY `ind-a Jersey foundation body`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)

`ind-a amb R` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

-- AMB-8 (S8.4-01). Expected: a company's principal address is its registered office ("if the registered charity is a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law
-- to have a registered office", src:240), whatever the caller says about what its constitutional Law requires. The encoding (F3.9 reading A, taken) reads the requirement into "company"
-- too, so with the requirement given as FALSE it falls through to 8(4)(b) and (c) and answers the governor's address.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `ind-a amb R` (`ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" `an applicant for registration` (LIST `a company`) TRUE EMPTY EMPTY) (`Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE, `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS JUST "1 Bond Street, St Helier", `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING, `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS LIST "La Rue, St Ouen") EQUALS LIST "1 Bond Street, St Helier"

-- AMB-9 (S7.3-01). Expected: where the Commissioner presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit (forbidden by 7(3)(a)), public benefit is not established: FALSE.
-- The encoding (F2.10 reading A, taken) REFUSES: "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE EMPTY (LIST `ind-a education purpose`)) (`Determination of public benefit` WITH `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`, `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE, `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE, `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE, `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE, `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE, `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS FALSE, `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS TRUE, `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE, `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE)
